content:
{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0106",
  "reason": "Check disk space and warnings for files-not-saving complaint"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, I'm sorry you've had to ask more than once, and thanks for sticking with us. I found the cause: your laptop's drive is almost full. Only about 9 GB of 256 GB is free (3.5%), and when it gets that low Windows can't save files. Here's how to free up space:\n\n1. Empty the Recycle Bin, then delete anything in your Downloads folder you don't need.\n2. Open Settings > System > Storage > Temporary files. Select the temporary files and old Windows Update files, then click Remove.\n3. Make sure OneDrive Files On-Demand is turned on (right-click the OneDrive cloud icon > Settings > Sync and back up > Advanced settings > Files On-Demand). Your synced files will then stay in the cloud until you open them.\n4. Uninstall any apps you no longer use (Settings > Apps > Installed apps).\n\nYou'll need to clear about 17 GB so the laptop has at least 10% free. Reply here once you've done these steps and I'll check the space from my end. If it's still too full, I'll pass it on so we can look at a bigger drive or another fix.",
  "internal_note": "Checked BL-LT-0106 (Win 11 Pro, assigned to Leo Martins). It's online and checked in recently. Disk: 9.0 GB free of 256 GB (3.5%), with a low-disk warning. This matches the KB-017 symptom of files not saving. Account is active with no issues. Sent the user the KB-017 cleanup steps (Recycle Bin/Downloads, temp files and old update files, OneDrive Files On-Demand, uninstall unused apps). Next step: re-run check_device_status when the user replies. If it's still under 10% free after cleanup, escalate to Tier 2 per KB-017 (bigger drive or replacement). The user says this is their third request, so look for earlier tickets and follow up quickly.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-017"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
